  "findings": [
    "Java's core model is as claimed for ordinary leaves, notes, and empty packages: GraphvizImageBuilder prints direct leaves before child groups, Bibliotekon preserves createNode insertion order in a LinkedHashMap, DotStringFactory passes allNodes to every solved edge, and SvekEdge.manageCollision mutates each endpoint label after each intersecting node.",
    "Rust's new collision-only slot projection follows svek_node_emission_order without globally reordering renderer-owned positions. The two declaration-order variants produce the same Java endpoint coordinates and the same Rust endpoint coordinates, supporting that narrow ordering change.",
    "The required shipped-path perturbation gate is nevertheless red. Both declaration-order variants fail on only the same endpoint label: Java x=183.6233 versus Rust x=183.6014. checker_nested_direct_before_group_tb independently fails on only its tail label, Java x=133.0945 versus Rust x=133.1256. These are valid, in-scope endpoint-collision outputs, not syntax pages or fixture metadata.",
    "The account's broader unified-stream claim is incomplete for association points. AbstractClassOrObjectDiagram.Association constructs the POINT_FOR_ASSOCIATION Entity at the association statement, under the shared endpoint parent when possible; GraphvizImageBuilder later encounters that point in ordinary package or root leaf order. Rust's SvekNodeEmission has no association-point variant and svek_collision_layout_slots unconditionally chains all association slots after every entity, note, and empty-package slot.",
    "The minimal root association control passes, so its geometry did not activate a noncommutative point collision. The nested association probes fail much earlier in layout and cannot isolate collision order. The source-level stream mismatch remains real, but the primary rejection does not rely on those confounded outputs.",
    "Plain attached-note and empty-package controls pass in both routing directions exercised. This supports those stream members rather than merely finding universal failures.",
    "The removed-leaf probe exposes separate lifecycle semantics and is not used as the primary rejection. It is preserved because the checker was instructed to probe hidden or omitted participants and preserve every result.",
    "Static inspection found no fixture labels, perturbation filenames, golden reads, SVG post-processing, coordinate-keyed conditionals, new parity constants, comparator changes, or frozen-control changes in the implementation diff.",
    "All 13 Java SVGs are well-formed XML and contain no recognized PlantUML syntax or error-page markers. Every run used the pinned Java revision and immutable binary identities, with no Cargo or rustc invocation."
  ],
